{"title":"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_OmegaLearn.org\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by OmegaLearn.org</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3_by_MadMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3 by MadMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the greatest possible area of the triangle in the complex plane with vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/2/612cb53032b6b7359a67ad3d622a6b2208728afa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2z$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/7/b77c4a59e7daec4e268cde48c5ee464e1a5fb1b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+i)z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07dc4fac5dd9ee692982bfc49f05aaebd536cd2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1-i)z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a complex number satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/6/a56b3e9bbd49337a9fff73708a44cea15b9014f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|4z - 2| = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/9/209586a21ce4206cabdd379cd1aa609a4daab3c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}~\\frac 14 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}~\\frac 12 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}~\\frac{9}{16} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}~\\frac 34 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}~1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"376\" height=\"38\" /> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because we can factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> from each vertex, the area of the triangle is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/c/92c5c761d6ec8b0fd28b5f8118fa50669a6549d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z|^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"21\" /> multiplied by the area of the triangle with vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/d/ebdd6b9d92b076aee5a8323c0ba727509d9fea2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 1+i, 1-i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"17\" />. \n</p><p>The vertical side of that triangle has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the altitude to that side has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We now just need the maximum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/c/92c5c761d6ec8b0fd28b5f8118fa50669a6549d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z|^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>The equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/7/ad7e58b4f62e0358f2e45a1c7bb17f078e4fbab9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|4z-2| = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" /> can be rewritten as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/8/478de3bf673d9993a61fcdfa3aa605ca5272c777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z-1/2| = 1/4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore, it exists as a circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/8/8f88d403085fe6600059002646348a5f267266d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" /> and center at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/5/015e9634e7ed01b2a7e9374f57cb92c505ad470c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1/2, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" /> on the complex plane. The maximum possible magnitude of a complex number on this circle occurs with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e1150a17bf1b733cb666be84d920c71fc96bb3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" />, with magnitude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e1150a17bf1b733cb666be84d920c71fc96bb3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" />. We can justify this because the line connecting the origin and the complex number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e1150a17bf1b733cb666be84d920c71fc96bb3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" /> goes through the center of the circle.\n</p><p>Our answer is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/e/ece36b17b91a8293044afeb423d07ca692bcc254.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)^2 = \\boxed{\\frac{9}{16}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"111\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~lprado\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rewrite the second and the third complex number, we get: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/2/f327a31b11d478ceace6bf8017126b4796c7a9de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}e^{i\\frac{\\pi}{4}}z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/4/bc4f9d77e859f33203850c2fdd0e33fce2c85ac7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}e^{-i\\frac{\\pi}{4}}z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"21\" />. This means that the other two complex numbers both form a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/1/821d3f11ab7a3e93c7a404a34224228f0449505a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> angle with complex numbers both form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/2/612cb53032b6b7359a67ad3d622a6b2208728afa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2z$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />. Also notice that the magnitude of the first complex number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/d/04de746d0a8bb3abab9b8b6bb008c5baa14c5a87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2|z|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"20\" />, and the second and third complex numbers both have magnitude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/b/14ba21162f7e19d2086ab748a84ef8993f753a6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}|z|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"45\" height=\"24\" />, this means that these three points form an isosceles right triangle. Therefore the area for this triangle is simply just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/c/c0ca3acc95abf295ce1d2b89d423288b40a3bf98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\sqrt{2}|z|\\cdot\\sqrt{2}|z|=|z|^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"179\" height=\"38\" />. \nNow since we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/b/41be32d7e612647550c977e80df5214b1919dbb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|4z-2|=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" />, we can set \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/e/2ae2993c7c2d9e646793ca3184bb378a2a806935.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4z-2=e^{i\\theta},\\theta\\in[0,2\\pi)\\]\" width=\"181\" height=\"20\" />\nTherefore\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/a/eea1ed4540dd916db357a6a1539dc86a4d108231.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z=\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{e^{i\\theta}}{4}\\]\" width=\"91\" height=\"39\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/c/75c21a02b82e5f3dd73fe5d4ee4ab8990df06635.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|z|=\\frac{1}{4}|2+e^{i\\theta}|=\\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{5+4\\cos\\theta}\\le\\frac{3}{4}\\]\" width=\"285\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/3/843622567e12d686e4e2f94ddfcb444e8ecde0d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/1/b61166da81797df75f636abad60d87f7f8a6c5c1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Area\\le \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} \\ \\frac{9}{16}}\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c3rKwSah-_A\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c3rKwSah-_A</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_OmegaLearn.org\">Video Solution 2 by OmegaLearn.org</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by OmegaLearn.org\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zbs5fnbOnpU\">https://youtu.be/zbs5fnbOnpU</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3_by_MadMath\">Video Solution 3 by MadMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3 by MadMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/uMBIZcQfCyY\">https://youtu.be/uMBIZcQfCyY</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B\">2025 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=